const body = "The upstream Pkl manager sounds good to me. Updating literal package URLs seems like a reasonable, bounded operation even though general automated editing of Pkl is more complicated.

One clarification: hk is generally backward compatible with older configs, so the version in `hk.pkl` doesn't need to match the executable version. An older schema/builtins pin isn't necessarily a problem, and using `hk = "latest"` is a valid choice. Keeping both pins current is a useful convenience for people who want it, but synchronization is optional.

Agreed on holding off on a preset here while the upstream proposal is considered. Thanks for working on this!

_This comment was generated by Codex._";
